    ($SATQ$d1482e27$SATQ$, $SATQ$640f84ff-2e95-4663-a2b0-f76527045992$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$Reading and Writing$SATQ$, $SATQ$Standard English Conventions$SATQ$, $SATQ$SEC$SATQ$, $SATQ$FSS$SATQ$, $SATQ$Form, Structure, and Sense$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 1, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>One of the earliest known maps is a Babylonian clay tablet thought to be almost 4,500 years old. The map <span aria-hidden="true">______</span><span class="sr-only">blank</span> the area of a plot of land, shows a river valley, and includes the cardinal directions.</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$<p>Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"1bb7a823-a8df-479a-ba69-52e6b6e72d17","content":"<p>describes</p>"},{"id":"bb7f5e2b-9913-4152-bfc7-68a615cd800c","content":"<p>describe</p>"},{"id":"38f24999-88eb-49b4-bbc7-7617d5e73290","content":"<p>have described</p>"},{"id":"53e06933-7f72-4ee7-b7c3-667d8a44b9ca","content":"<p>are describing</p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["1bb7a823-a8df-479a-ba69-52e6b6e72d17"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice A is the best answer. The convention being tested is the use of verb forms within a sentence. The singular verb "describes" agrees in number with the singular subject "map."</p><p>Choice B is incorrect because the plural verb "describe" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the singular subject "map." Choice C is incorrect because the plural verb "have described" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the singular subject "map." Choice D is incorrect because the plural verb "are describing" doesn&rsquo;t agree in number with the singular subject "map."</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"d1482e27","external_id":"640f84ff-2e95-4663-a2b0-f76527045992","vaultid":null,"uId":"fac28f59-bc5e-479d-9dce-596abb5784e5","program":"SAT","test_type":1,"test_type_desc":"Reading and Writing","primary_class_c